1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:02,610
(Penny:)I didn't know you had company.
I don't want to impose.

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:04,530
(Sheldon:)No, no. It's not
an imposition.

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:07,880
(Sheldon:)At this point, in our ecosystem,
you are akin to the plover,

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,890
(Sheldon:)a small scavenging bird
that eats extra food

5
00:00:10,890 --> 00:00:12,850
(Sheldon:)from between
the teeth of crocodiles.

6
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,860
(Sheldon:)Please, fly into our open maw,
and have at it.

7
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:22,560
(Penny:)If I had more than a box of
baking soda in my refrigerator,

8
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,930
(Penny:)I wouldn't have to take that.

9
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:29,540
(Amy:)Hi, bestie.

10
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:30,940
(Bernadette:)Hi.

11
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:35,210
(Penny:)So, um, Priya,

12
00:00:35,210 --> 00:00:36,510
(Penny:)you're a lawyer, right?

13
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,210
(Priya:)I know. Pretty boring, huh?

14
00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:41,450
(Leonard:)Oh, come on.
It's not boring at all.

15
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:44,850
(Leonard:)She's currently helping set up
a secondary derivative market

16
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:47,360
(Leonard:)which would allow
overseas car firms

17
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,820
(Leonard:)to hedge their investments

18
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,490
(Leonard:)against potential advancements
in battery technology.

19
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:52,780
(Leonard:)Hmm?

20
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:54,330
(Priya:)Thank you, Leonard.

21
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,700
(Priya:)That doesn't make it
sound boring at all.

22
00:00:58,270 --> 00:01:00,800
(Amy:)So, how you holding up?

